    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I've got a heifer that just came out of rumenotomy an hour ago. Can u give me a quick rundown of what i should be looking out for over the next few days regarding infection and when i can start getting her back on feed?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Right now, your heifer needs careful monitoring, especially since she just had a rumenotomy. Look for signs of infection like excessive swelling around the incision, foul-smelling discharge, or fever. Keep an eye on her appetite and overall demeanor; if she seems lethargic or is refusing to eat, that's a red flag. You should consult with your veterinarian before reintroducing feed, as the timing depends on how well the surgical site is healing. Generally, they will want to ensure the incision is stable before allowing a full return to normal feeding.",
